Problem:
Find all lists $\left(x_{1}, x_{2}, \ldots, x_{2020}\right) $ of nonnegative real numbers to satisfy all three of the following conditions:
(i) $x_{1} \leq x_{2} \leq \ldots \leq x_{2020}$;
(ii) $x_{2020} \leq x_{1}+1$;
(iii) there is a permutation $\left(y_{1}, y_{2}, \ldots, y_{2020}\right) $ from $\left(x_{1}, x_{2}, \ldots, x_{2020}\right) $ such that:
$$
\sum_{i=1}^{2020}\left(\left(x_{i}+1\right) \left(y_{i}+1\right) \right) ^{2}=8 \sum_{i=1}^{2020} x_{i}^{3}
$$
A list permutation is a list of the same length, with the same entries, but entries can be in any order. For example $(2, 1, 2) $ is a permutation $(1, 2, 2) $ and both are permutations $(2, 2, 1) $. Note that each list is a permutation of itself.

